If a clinician treats a patient in a supervised-setting and the patient receives a regular-buprenorphine-dosage then the clinician may add a short-acting-full-agonist-opioid to the regular-buprenorphine-dosage for the patient and may continue the regular-buprenorphine-dosage for the patient.
If a clinician makes a buprenorphine-discontinuation-decision for a patient then the clinician should conduct a close-patient-monitoring for the patient and should monitor the patient for an oversedation and should monitor the patient for a respiratory-depression.
